        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google): register 'google' alias for memory embedding provider",
        "body": "fix(google): register 'google' alias for memory embedding provider\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nUsers configure `memorySearch.provider: \"google\"` but the Google memory embedding provider is registered with id `\"gemini\"` only. This causes \"Unknown memory embedding provider: google\" errors at runtime.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRegister a second provider entry with `id: \"google\"` so both `\"gemini\"` and `\"google\"` resolve to the Gemini embedding provider.\n\nFixes #90786.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource verification showing both provider IDs are now registered:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx -e \"\nimport fs from 'fs';\nconst src = fs.readFileSync('extensions/google/index.ts','utf8');\nconst lines = src.split('\\n');\nfor(let i=0;i<lines.length;i++){\n    if(lines[i].includes('registerMemoryEmbeddingProvider')){\n        console.log('Line '+(i+1)+': '+lines[i].trim());\n    }\n}\n\"\nLine 346: api.registerMemoryEmbeddingProvider(geminiMemoryEmbeddingProviderAdapter);\nLine 347: api.registerMemoryEmbeddingProvider({ ...geminiMemoryEmbeddingProviderAdapter, id: \"google\" });\n```\n\nTargeted test:\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/google/index.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  77 passed (77)\n  Duration  23.15s\n```\n\nFormatting:\n\n```text\n$ npx oxfmt --check extensions/google/index.ts\nChecking formatting...\n\nAll matched files use the correct format.\nFinished in 65ms on 1 files using 8 threads.\n```\n\nWhitespace:\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check\n```",
